prs.body:
Report nested functions that only reference a more distant ancestor, matching Unicorn. For example, `inner` below was previously allowed and now reports that it can move to the outer scope:

```js
const shared = 1;
function outer() {
    function inner() {
        return shared;
    }
    return inner();
}
```

Include parameter defaults in capture checks so functions that depend on parent variables or lexical `this` remain nested. Preserve captures in parents with direct eval and Unicorn's handling of variables used directly by the parent. Cache each ancestor symbol's referencing scopes once per file, shared across candidate functions.

Fixes #26591
